htly simplified\nsince the input is assumed to be a string rather than an arbitrary byte\nstream.\n\nTake an IRI (string or UT", "start_line": 118, "end_line": 147, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "uri_to_iri", "qualified_name": "uri_to_iri", "args": ["uri"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert a Uniform Resource Identifier(URI) into an Internationalized\nResource Identifier(IRI).\n\nThis is the algorithm from section 3.2 of RFC 3987, excluding step 4.\n\nTake an URI in ASCII bytes (e.g. '/I%20%E2%99%A5%20Django/') and return\na string containing the encoded result (e.g. '/I%20\u2665%20Django", "start_line": 168, "end_line": 201, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "escape_uri_path", "qualified_name": "escape_uri_path", "args": ["path"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Escape the unsafe characters from the path portion of a Uniform Resource\nIdentifier (URI).", "start_line": 204, "end_line": 218, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "repercent_broken_unicode", "qualified_name": "repercent_broken_unicode", "args": ["path"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "As per section 3.2 of RFC 3987, step three of converting a URI into an IRI,\nrepercent-encode any octet produced that is not part of a strictly legal\nUTF-8 octet sequence.", "start_line": 221, "end_line": 233, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "filepath_to_uri", "qualified_name": "filepath_to_uri", "args": ["path"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert a file system path to a URI portion that is suitable for\ninclusion in a URL.\n\nEncode certain chars that would normally be recognized as special chars\nfor URIs. Do not encode the ' character, as it is a valid character\nwithin URIs. See the encodeURIComponent() JavaScript function for details.", "start_line": 236, "end_line": 248, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_system_encoding", "qualified_name": "get_system_encoding", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The encoding of 