s method must be implemented by a subclass.**", "start_line": 97, "end_line": 106, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_prepare_messages", "qualified_name": "_prepare_messages", "args": ["self", "messages"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Prepare a list of messages for storage.", "start_line": 108, "end_line": 113, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "update", "qualified_name": "update", "args": ["self", "response"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Store all unread messages.\n\nIf the backend has yet to be iterated, store previously stored messages\nagain. Otherwise, only store messages added after the last iteration.", "start_line": 115, "end_line": 127, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add", "qualified_name": "add", "args": ["self", "level", "message", "extra_tags"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Queue a message to be stored.\n\nThe message is only queued if it contained something and its level is\nnot less than the recording level (``self.level``).", "start_line": 129, "end_line": 145, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_level", "qualified_name": "_get_level", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the minimum recorded level.\n\nThe default level is the ``MESSAGE_LEVEL`` setting. If this is\nnot found, the ``INFO`` level is used.", "start_line": 147, "end_line": 156, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_set_level", "qualified_name": "_set_level", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set a custom minimum recorded level.\n\nIf set to ``None``, the default level will be used (see the\n``_get_level`` method).", "start_line": 158, "end_line": 168, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "Message", "bases": [], "methods": ["__init__", "_prepare", "__eq__", "__str__", "tags", "level_tag"], "docstring": "Represent an actual message that can be stored in any of the supported\nstorage classes (typically session- or cookie-based) and 