es not address the\nmore general issue of opening a file for writing and reading in multiple\nprocesses in a manner that works across platforms.\n\nThe custom version of NamedTemporaryFile doesn't support the same keyword\narguments available in tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile.\n\n1: https://mail.python.org/pipermail/python-list/2005-December/336957.html\n2: https://bugs.python.org/issue14243", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "django/core/files/utils.py", "file_hash": "e40772e89bb30986ff540b52c1cf43afe8939a9b8c215b89dd129c935fac6339", "imports": [], "functions": [{"name": "closed", "qualified_name": "closed", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 27, "end_line": 28, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "readable", "qualified_name": "readable", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 30, "end_line": 35, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "writable", "qualified_name": "writable", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 37, "end_line": 42, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "seekable", "qualified_name": "seekable", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 44, "end_line": 49, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__iter__", "qualified_name": "__iter__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 51, "end_line": 52, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}], "classes": [{"name": "FileProxyMixin", "bases": [], "methods": ["closed", "readable", "writable", "seekable", "__iter__"], "docstring": "A mixin class used to forward file methods to an underlaying file\nobject.  The internal file object has to be called \"file\"::\n\n    class FileProxy(FileProxyMixin):\n        def __init__(self, file):\n            self.file = file", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 52}], "calls": [], "module_docstring": "", "parse_error": ""}, {"file_path": "django/core/files/storage.py", "file_hash": "a403777e94