 "end_line": 256, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__iter__", "qualified_name": "__iter__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The queryset iterator protocol uses three nested iterators in the\ndefault case:\n    1. sql.compiler.execute_sql()\n       - Returns 100 rows at time (constants.GET_ITERATOR_CHUNK_SIZE)\n         using cursor.fetchmany(). This part is responsible for\n         doing some column masking, and returning th", "start_line": 258, "end_line": 274, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__bool__", "qualified_name": "__bool__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 276, "end_line": 278, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__getitem__", "qualified_name": "__getitem__", "args": ["self", "k"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Retrieve an item or slice from the set of results.", "start_line": 280, "end_line": 308, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__and__", "qualified_name": "__and__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 310, "end_line": 319, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__or__", "qualified_name": "__or__", "args": ["self", "other"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 321, "end_line": 333, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_iterator", "qualified_name": "_iterator", "args": ["self", "use_chunked_fetch", "chunk_size"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 339, "end_line": 340, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "iterator", "qualified_name": "iterator", "args": ["self", "chunk_size"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "An iterator over the results from applying this QuerySet to the\ndatabase.", "start_line": 342, "end_line": 350, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "aggregate", "qualified_name": "aggregate", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a dictionary containing the calculations (aggregation)\nover the current queryset.\n\nIf args is present the expression is passed as a kwarg using\nthe Aggregate object's default alias.", "start_line": 352, "end_line": 378, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "count", "qualified_name": "count", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Perform a SELECT COUNT() and return the number of records as an\ninteger.\n\nIf the QuerySet is already fully cached, return the length of the\ncached results set to avoid multiple SELECT COUNT(*) calls.", "start_line": 380, "end_line": 391, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get", "qualified_name": "get", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Perform the query and return a single object matching the given\nkeyword arguments.", "start_line": 393, "end_line": 412, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "create", "qualified_name": "create", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create a new object with the given kwargs, saving it to the database\nand returning the created object.", "start_line": 414, "end_line": 422, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_populate_pk_values", "qualified_name": "_populate_pk_values", "args": ["self", "objs"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 424, "end_line": 427, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "bulk_create", "qualified_name": "bulk_create", "args": ["self", "objs", "batch_size", "ignore_conflicts"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Insert each of the instances into the database. Do *not* call\nsave() on each of the instances, do not send any pre/post_save\nsignals, and do not set the primary key attribute if it is an\nautoincrement field (except if features.can_return_rows_from_bulk_insert=True).\nMulti-table models are not suppor", "start_line": 429, "end_line": 481, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "bulk_update", "qualified_name": "bulk_update", "args": ["self", "objs", "fields", "batch_size"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Update the given fields in each of the given objects in the database.", "start_line": 483, "end_line": 524, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_or_create", "qualified_name": "get_or_create", "args": ["self", "defaults"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Look up an object with the given kwargs, creating one if necessary.\nReturn a tuple of (object, created), where created is a boolean\nspecifying whether an object was created.", "start_line": 527, "end_line": 540, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "update_or_create", "qualified_name": "update_or_create", "args": ["self", "defaults"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Look up an object with the given kwargs, updating one with defaults\nif it exists, otherwise create a new one.\nReturn a tuple (object, created), where created is a boolean\nspecifying whether an object was created.", "start_line": 542, "end_line": 564, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_create_object_from_params", "qualified_name": "_create_object_from_params", "args": ["self", "lookup", "params", "lock"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Try to create an object using passed params. Used by get_or_create()\nand update_or_create().", "start_line": 566, "end_line": 582, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_extract_model_params", "qualified_name": "_extract_model_params", "args": ["self", "defaults"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Prepare `params` for creating a model instance based on the given\nkwargs; for use by get_or_create() and update_or_create().", "start_line": 584, "end_line": 607, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_earliest", "qualified_name": "_earliest", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the earliest object according to fields (if given) or by the\nmodel's Meta.get_latest_by.", "start_line": 609, "end_line": 632, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "earliest", "qualified_name": "earliest", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 634, "end_line": 635, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "latest", "qualified_name": "latest", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 637, "end_line": 638, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "first", "qualified_name": "first", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the first object of a query or None if no match is found.", "start_line": 640, "end_line": 643, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "last", "qualified_name": "last", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the last object of a query or None if no match is found.", "start_line": 645, "end_line": 648, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "in_bulk", "qualified_name": "in_bulk", "args": ["self", "id_list"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a dictionary mapping each of the given IDs to the object with\nthat ID. If `id_list` isn't provided, evaluate the entire QuerySet.", "start_line": 650, "end_line": 676, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "delete", "qualified_name": "delete", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Delete the records in the current QuerySet.", "start_line": 678, "end_line": 704, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_raw_delete", "qualified_name": "_raw_delete", "args": ["self", "using"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Delete objects found from the given queryset in single direct SQL\nquery. No signals are sent and there is no protection for cascades.", "start_line": 709, "end_line": 714, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "update", "qualified_name": "update", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Update all elements in the current QuerySet, setting all the given\nfields to the appropriate values.", "start_line": 717, "end_line": 732, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_update", "qualified_name": "_update", "args": ["self", "values"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A version of update(