 "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given a cursor object that has just performed an INSERT...RETURNING\nstatement into a table that has an auto-incrementing ID, return the\nnewly created ID.", "start_line": 176, "end_line": 182, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "field_cast_sql", "qualified_name": "field_cast_sql", "args": ["self", "db_type", "internal_type"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given a column type (e.g. 'BLOB', 'VARCHAR') and an internal type\n(e.g. 'GenericIPAddressField'), return the SQL to cast it before using\nit in a WHERE statement. The resulting string should contain a '%s'\nplaceholder for the column being searched against.", "start_line": 184, "end_line": 191, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "force_no_ordering", "qualified_name": "force_no_ordering", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list used in the \"ORDER BY\" clause to force no ordering at\nall. Return an empty list to include nothing in the ordering.", "start_line": 193, "end_line": 198, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "for_update_sql", "qualified_name": "for_update_sql", "args": ["self", "nowait", "skip_locked", "of"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the FOR UPDATE SQL clause to lock rows for an update operation.", "start_line": 200, "end_line": 208, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_limit_offset_params", "qualified_name": "_get_limit_offset_params", "args": ["self", "low_mark", "high_mark"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 210, "end_line": 216, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "limit_offset_sql", "qualified_name": "limit_offset_sql", "args": ["self", "low_mark", "high_mark"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return LIMIT/OFFSET SQL clause.", "start_line": 218, "end_line": 224, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "last_executed_query", "qualified_name": "last_executed_query", "args": ["self", "cursor", "sql", "params"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a string of the query last executed by the given cursor, with\nplaceholders replaced with actual values.\n\n`sql` is the raw query containing placeholders and `params` is the\nsequence of parameters. These are used by default, but this method\nexists for database backends to provide a better imple", "start_line": 226, "end_line": 246, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "last_insert_id", "qualified_name": "last_insert_id", "args": ["self", "cursor", "table_name", "pk_name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Given a cursor object that has just performed an INSERT statement into\na table that has an auto-incrementing ID, return the newly created ID.\n\n`pk_name` is the name of the primary-key column.", "start_line": 248, "end_line": 255, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "lookup_cast", "qualified_name": "lookup_cast", "args": ["self", "lookup_type", "internal_type"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the string to use in a query when performing lookups\n(\"contains\", \"like\", etc.). It should contain a '%s' placeholder for\nthe column being searched against.", "start_line": 257, "end_line": 263, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "max_in_list_size", "qualified_name": "max_in_list_size", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the maximum number of items that can be passed in a single 'IN'\nlist condition, or None if the backend does not impose a limit.", "start_line": 265, "end_line": 270, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "max_name_length", "qualified_name": "max_name_length", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the maximum length of table and column names, or None if there\nis no limit.", "start_line": 272, "end_line": 277, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "no_limit_value", "qualified_name": "no_limit_value", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the value to use for the LIMIT when we are wanting \"LIMIT\ninfinity\". Return None if the limit clause can be omitted in this case.", "start_line": 279, "end_line": 284, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pk_default_value", "qualified_name": "pk_default_value", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the value to use during an INSERT statement to specify that\nthe field should use its default value.", "start_line": 286, "end_line": 291, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "prepare_sql_script", "qualified_name": "prepare_sql_script", "args": ["self", "sql"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Take an SQL script that may contain multiple lines and return a list\nof statements to feed to successive cursor.execute() calls.\n\nSince few databases are able to process raw SQL scripts in a single\ncursor.execute() call and PEP 249 doesn't talk about this use case,\nthe default implementation is cons", "start_line": 293, "end_line": 305, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "process_clob", "qualified_name": "process_clob", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the value of a CLOB column, for backends that return a locator\nobject that requires additional processing.", "start_line": 307, "end_line": 312, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "return_insert_id", "qualified_name": "return_insert_id", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "For backends that support returning the last insert ID as part of an\ninsert query, return the SQL and params to append to the INSERT query.\nThe returned fragment should contain a format string to hold the\nappropriate column.", "start_line": 314, "end_line": 321, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "compiler", "qualified_name": "compiler", "args": ["self", "compiler_name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the SQLCompiler class corresponding to the given name,\nin the namespace corresponding to the `compiler_module` attribute\non this backend.", "start_line": 323, "end_line": 331, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "quote_name", "qualified_name": "quote_name", "args": ["self", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a quoted version of the given table, index, or column name. Do\nnot quote the given name if it's already been quoted.", "start_line": 333, "end_line": 338, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "random_function_sql", "qualified_name": "random_function_sql", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return an SQL expression that returns a random value.", "start_line": 340, "end_line": 342, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "regex_lookup", "qualified_name": "regex_lookup", "args": ["self", "lookup_type"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the string to use in a query when performing regular expression\nlookups (using \"regex\" or \"iregex\"). It should contain a '%s'\nplaceholder for the column being searched against.\n\nIf the feature is not supported (or part of it is not supported), raise\nNotImplementedError.", "start_line": 344, "end_line": 353, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "savepoint_create_sql", "qualified_name": "savepoint_create_sql", "args": ["self", "sid"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the SQL for starting a new savepoint. Only required if the\n\"uses_savepoints\" feature is True. The \"sid\" parameter is a string\nfor the savepoint id.", "start_line": 355, "end_line": 361, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "savepoint_commit_sql", "qualified_name": "savepoint_commit_sql", "args": ["self", "sid"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the SQL for committing the given savepoint.", "start_line": 363, "end_line": 367, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "savepoint_rollback_sql", "qualified_name": "savepoint_rollback_sql", "args": ["self", "sid"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the SQL for rolling back the given savepoint.", "start_line": 369, "end_line": 373, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_time_zone_sql", "qualified_name": "set_time_zone_sql", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the SQL that will set the connection's time zone.\n\nReturn '' if the backend doesn't support time zones.", "start_line": 375, "end_line": 381, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "sql_flush", "qualified_name": "sql_flush", "args": ["self", "style", "tables", "sequences", "allow_cascade"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of SQL statements required to remove all data from\nthe given database tables (without actually removing the tables\nthemselves) and the SQL statements required to reset the sequences\npassed in `sequences`.\n\nThe `style` argument is a Style object as returned by either\ncolor_style() or no", "start_line": 383, "end_line": 397, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "execute_sql_flush", "qualified_name": "execute_sql_flush", "args": ["self", "using", "sql_list"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Execute a list of SQL statements to flush the database.", "start_line": 399, "end_line": 404, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "sequence_reset_by_name_sql", "qualified_name": "sequence_reset_by_name_sql", "args": ["self", "style", "sequences"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of the SQL statements required to reset sequences\npassed in `sequences`.\n\nThe `style` argument is a Style object as returned by either\ncolor_style() or no_style() in django.core.management.color.", "start_line": 406, "end_line": 414, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "sequence_reset_sql", "qualified_name": "sequence_reset_sql", "args": ["self", "style", "model_list"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of the SQL statements required to reset sequences for\nthe given models.\n\nThe `style` argument is a Style object as returned by either\ncolor_style() or no_style() in django.core.management.color.", "start_line": 416, "end_line": 424, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "start_transaction_sql", "qualified_name": "start_transaction_sql", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the SQL statement required to start a transaction.", "start_line": 426, "end_line": 428, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "end_transaction_sql", "qualified_name": "end_transaction_sql", "args": ["self", "success"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the SQL statement required to end a transaction.", "start_line": 430, "end_line": 434, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "tablespace_sql", "qualified_name": "tablespace_sql", "args": ["self", "tablespace", "inline"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the SQL that will be used in a query to define the tablespace.\n\nReturn '' if the backend doesn't support tablespaces.\n\nIf `inline` is True, append the SQL to a row; otherwise append it to\nthe entire CREATE TABLE or CREATE INDEX statement.", "start_line": 436, "end_line": 445, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "prep_for_like_query", "qualified_name": "prep_for_like_query", "args": ["self", "x"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Prepare a value for use in a LIKE query.", "start_line": 447, "end_line": 449, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "validate_autopk_value", "qualified_name": "validate_autopk_value", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Certain backends do not accept some values for \"serial\" fields\n(for example zero in MySQL). Raise a ValueError if the value is\ninvalid, otherwise return the validated value.", "start_line": 455, "end_line": 461, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "adapt_unknown_value", "qualified_name": "adapt_unknown_value", "args": ["self", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Transform a value to something compatible with the backend driver.\n\nThis method only depends on the type of the value. It's designed for\ncases where the target type isn't known, such as .raw() SQL queries.\nAs a consequence it may no