ted\n[\"foo\", \"bar\"] format.", "start_line": 354, "end_line": 368, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "alter_index_together", "qualified_name": "alter_index_together", "args": ["self", "model", "old_index_together", "new_index_together"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Deal with a model changing its index_together. The input\nindex_togethers must be doubly-nested, not the single-nested\n[\"foo\", \"bar\"] format.", "start_line": 370, "end_line": 384, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_delete_composed_index", "qualified_name": "_delete_composed_index", "args": ["self", "model", "fields", "constraint_kwargs", "sql"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 386, "end_line": 395, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "alter_db_table", "qualified_name": "alter_db_table", "args": ["self", "model", "old_db_table", "new_db_table"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Rename the table a model points to.", "start_line": 397, "end_line": 410, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "alter_db_tablespace", "qualified_name": "alter_db_tablespace", "args": ["self", "model", "old_db_tablespace", "new_db_tablespace"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Move a model's table between tablespaces.", "start_line": 412, "end_line": 418, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_field", "qualified_name": "add_field", "args": ["self", "model", "field"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create a field on a model. Usually involves adding a column, but may\ninvolve adding a table instead (for M2M fields).", "start_line": 420, "end_line": 473, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "remove_field", "qualified_name": "remove_field", "args": ["self", "model", "field"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Remove a field from a model. Usually involves deleting a column,\nbut for M2Ms may involve deleting a table.", "start_line": 475, "end_line": 503, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "alter_field", "qualified_name": "alter_field", "args": ["self", "model", "old_field", "new_field", "strict"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Allow a field's type, uniqueness, nullability, default, column,\nconstraints, etc. to be modified.\n`old_field` is required to compute the necessary changes.\nIf `strict` is True, raise errors if the old column does not match\n`old_field` precisely.", "start_line": 505, "end_line": 544, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_alter_field", "qualified_name": "_alter_field", "args": ["self", "model", "old_field", "new_field", "old_type", "new_type", "old_db_params", "new_db_params", "strict"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Perform a \"physical\" (non-ManyToMany) field update.", "start_line": 546, "end_line": 778, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_alter_column_null_sql", "qualified_name": "_alter_column_null_sql", "args": ["self", "model", "old_field", "new_field"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Hook to specialize column null alteration.\n\nReturn a (sql, params) fragment to set a column to null or non-null\nas required by new_field, or None if no changes are required.", "start_line": 780, "end_line": 800, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_alter_column_default_sql", "qualified_name": "_alter_column_default_sql", "args": ["self", "model", "old_field", "new_field", "drop"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Hook to specialize column default alteration.\n\nReturn a (sql, params) fragment to add or drop (depending on the drop\nargument) a default to new_field's column.", "start_line": 802, "end_line": 831, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_alter_column_type_sql", "qualified_name": "_alter_column_type_sql", "args": ["self", "model", "old_field", "new_field", "new_type"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Hook to specialize column type alteration for different backends,\nfor cases when a creation type is different to an alteration type\n(e.g. SERIAL in PostgreSQL, PostGIS fields).\n\nReturn a two-tuple of: an SQL fragment of (sql, params) to insert into\nan ALTER TABLE statement and a list of extra (sql, ", "start_line": 833, "end_line": 852, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_alter_many_to_many", "qualified_name": "_alter_many_to_many", "args": ["self", "model", "old_field", "new_field", "strict"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Alter M2Ms to repoint their to= endpoints.", "start_line": 854, "end_line": 873, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_create_index_name", "qualified_name": "_create_index_name", "args": ["self", "table_name", "column_names", "suffix"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Generate a unique name for an index/unique constraint.\n\nThe name is divided into 3 parts: the table name, the column names,\nand a unique digest and suffix.", "start_line": 875, "end_line": 902, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_index_tablespace_sql", "qualified_name": "_get_index_tablespace_sql", "args": ["self", "model", "fields", "db_tablespace"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 904, "end_line": 912, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_create_index_sql", "qualified_name": "_create_index_sql", "args": ["self", "model", "fields"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the SQL statement to create the index for one or several fields.\n`sql` can be specified if the syntax differs from the standard (GIS\nindexes, ...).", "start_line": 914, "end_line": 941, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_delete_index_sql", "qualified_name": "_delete_index_sql", "args": ["self", "model", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 943, "end_line": 948, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_index_columns", "qualified_name": "_index_columns", "args": ["self", "table", "columns", "col_suffixes", "opclasses"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 950, "end_line": 951, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_model_indexes_sql", "qualified_name": "