9, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_prefetch_queryset", "qualified_name": "get_prefetch_queryset", "args": ["self", "instances", "queryset"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 111, "end_line": 140, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_object", "qualified_name": "get_object", "args": ["self", "instance"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 142, "end_line": 145, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__get__", "qualified_name": "__get__", "args": ["self", "instance", "cls"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get the related instance through the forward relation.\n\nWith the example above, when getting ``child.parent``:\n\n- ``self`` is the descriptor managing the ``parent`` attribute\n- ``instance`` is the ``child`` instance\n- ``cls`` is the ``Child`` class (we don't need it)", "start_line": 147, "end_line": 192, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__set__", "qualified_name": "__set__", "args": ["self", "instance", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set the related instance through the forward relation.\n\nWith the example above, when setting ``child.parent = parent``:\n\n- ``self`` is the descriptor managing the ``parent`` attribute\n- ``instance`` is the ``child`` instance\n- ``value`` is the ``parent`` instance on the right of the equal sign", "start_line": 194, "end_line": 258, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__reduce__", "qualified_name": "__reduce__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Pickling should return the instance attached by self.field on the\nmodel, not a new copy of that descriptor. Use getattr() to retrieve\nthe instance directly from the model.", "start_line": 260, "end_line": 266, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_object", "qualified_name": "get_object", "args": ["self", "instance"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 281, "end_line": 298, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__set__", "qualified_name": "__set__", "args": ["self", "instance", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 300, "end_line": 314, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "related"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 330, "end_line": 333, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "RelatedObjectDoesNotExist", "qualified_name": "RelatedObjectDoesNotExist", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["cached_property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 336, "end_line": 348, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_cached", "qualified_name": "is_cached", "args": ["self", "instance"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 350, "end_line": 351, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_queryset", "qualified_name": "get_queryset", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 353, "end_line": 354, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_prefetch_queryset", "qualified_name": "get_prefetch_queryset", "args": ["self", "instances", "queryset"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 356, "end_line": 372, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__get__", "qualified_name": "__get__", "args": ["self", "instance", "cls"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get the related instance through the reverse relation.\n\nWith the example above, when getting ``place.restaurant``:\n\n- ``self`` is the descriptor managing the ``restaurant`` attribute\n- ``instance`` is the ``place`` instance\n- ``cls`` is the ``Place`` class (unused)\n\nKeep in mind that ``Restaurant`` ", "start_line": 374, "end_line": 419, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__set__", "qualified_name": "__set__", "args": ["self", "instance", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set the related instance through the reverse relation.\n\nWith the example above, when setting ``place.restaurant = restaurant``:\n\n- ``self`` is the descriptor managing the ``restaurant`` attribute\n- ``instance`` is the ``place`` instance\n- ``value`` is the ``restaurant`` instance on the right of the ", "start_line": 421, "end_line": 478, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__reduce__", "qualified_name": "__reduce__", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 480, "end_line": 482, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "rel"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 501, "end_line": 503, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "related_manager_cls", "qualified_name": "related_manager_cls", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["cached_property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 506, "end_line": 512, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__get__", "qualified_name": "__get__", "args": ["self", "instance", "cls"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get the related objects through the reverse relation.\n\nWith the example above, when getting ``parent.children``:\n\n- ``self`` is the descriptor managing the ``children`` attribute\n- ``instance`` is the ``parent`` instance\n- ``cls`` is the ``Parent`` class (unused)", "start_line": 514, "end_line": 527, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_get_set_deprecation_msg_params", "qualified_name": "_get_set_deprecation_msg_params", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 529, "end_line": 533, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__set__", "qualified_name": "__set__", "args": ["self", "instance", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 535, "end_line": 539, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "rel", "reverse"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 765, "end_line": 768, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "through", "qualified_name": "through", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["pr