sing get_lookup()\nand get_transform().", "start_line": 1071, "end_line": 1114, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "try_transform", "qualified_name": "try_transform", "args": ["self", "lhs", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Helper method for build_lookup(). Try to fetch and initialize\na transform for name parameter from lhs.", "start_line": 1116, "end_line": 1134, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "build_filter", "qualified_name": "build_filter", "args": ["self", "filter_expr", "branch_negated", "current_negated", "can_reuse", "allow_joins", "split_subq", "reuse_with_filtered_relation", "simple_col"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Build a WhereNode for a single filter clause but don't add it\nto this Query. Query.add_q() will then add this filter to the where\nNode.\n\nThe 'branch_negated' tells us if the current branch contains any\nnegations. This will be used to determine if subqueries are needed.\n\nThe 'current_negated' is used", "start_line": 1136, "end_line": 1255, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_filter", "qualified_name": "add_filter", "args": ["self", "filter_clause"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1257, "end_line": 1258, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_q", "qualified_name": "add_q", "args": ["self", "q_object"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A preprocessor for the internal _add_q(). Responsible for doing final\njoin promotion.", "start_line": 1260, "end_line": 1275, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "build_where", "qualified_name": "build_where", "args": ["self", "q_object"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1277, "end_line": 1278, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_add_q", "qualified_name": "_add_q", "args": ["self", "q_object", "used_aliases", "branch_negated", "current_negated", "allow_joins", "split_subq", "simple_col"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add a Q-object to the current filter.", "start_line": 1280, "end_line": 1306, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "build_filtered_relation_q", "qualified_name": "build_filtered_relation_q", "args": ["self", "q_object", "reuse", "branch_negated", "current_negated"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add a FilteredRelation object to the current filter.", "start_line": 1308, "end_line": 1328, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_filtered_relation", "qualified_name": "add_filtered_relation", "args": ["self", "filtered_relation", "alias"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1330, "end_line": 1341, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "names_to_path", "qualified_name": "names_to_path", "args": ["self", "names", "opts", "allow_many", "fail_on_missing"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Walk the list of names and turns them into PathInfo tuples. A single\nname in 'names' can generate multiple PathInfos (m2m, for example).\n\n'names' is the path of names to travel, 'opts' is the model Options we\nstart the name resolving from, 'allow_many' is as for setup_joins().\nIf fail_on_missing is ", "start_line": 1343, "end_line": 1437, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "setup_joins", "qualified_name": "setup_joins", "args": ["self", "names", "opts", "alias", "can_reuse", "allow_many", "reuse_with_filtered_relation"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Compute the necessary table joins for the passage through the fields\ngiven in 'names'. 'opts' is the Options class for the current model\n(which gives the table we are starting from), 'alias' is the alias for\nthe table to start the joining from.\n\nThe 'can_reuse' defines the reverse foreign key joins ", "start_line": 1439, "end_line": 1539, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "trim_joins", "qualified_name": "trim_joins", "args": ["self", "targets", "joins", "path"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "The 'target' parameter is the final field being joined to, 'joins'\nis the full list of join aliases. The 'path' contain the PathInfos\nused to create the joins.\n\nReturn the final target field and table alias and the new active\njoins.\n\nAlways trim any direct join if the target column is already in the", "start_line": 1541, "end_line": 1567, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "resolve_ref", "qualified_name": "resolve_ref", "args": ["self", "name", "allow_joins", "reuse", "summarize", "simple_col"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1569, "end_line": 1596, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "split_exclude", "qualified_name": "split_exclude", "args": ["self", "filter_expr", "can_reuse", "names_with_path"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "When doing an exclude against any kind of N-to-many relation, we need\nto use a subquery. This method constructs the nested query, given the\noriginal exclude filter (filter_expr) and the portion up to the first\nN-to-many relation field.\n\nFor example, if the origin filter is ~Q(child__name='foo'), fil", "start_line": 1598, "end_line": 1663, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_empty", "qualified_name": "set_empty", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1665, "end_line": 1666, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_empty", "qualified_name": "is_empty", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1668, "end_line": 1669, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_limits", "qualified_name": "set_limits", "args": ["self", "low", "high"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Adjust the limits on the rows retrieved. Use low/high to set these,\nas it makes it more Pythonic to read and write. When the SQL query is\ncreated, convert them to the appropriate offset and limit values.\n\nApply any limits passed in here to the existing constraints. Add low\nto the current low value a", "start_line": 1671, "end_line": 1692, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clear_limits", "qualified_name": "clear_limits", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Clear any existing limits.", "start_line": 1694, "end_line": 1696, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "has_limit_one", "qualified_name": "has_limit_one", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1698, "end_line": 1699, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "can_filter", "qualified_name": "can_filter", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return True if adding filters to this instance is still possible.\n\nTypically, this means no limits or offsets have been put on the results.", "start_line": 1701, "end_line": 1707, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clear_select_clause", "qualified_name": "clear_select_clause", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Remove all fields from SELECT clause.", "start_line": 1709, "end_line": 1715, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clear_select_fields", "qualified_name": "clear_select_fields", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Clear the list of fields to select (but not extra_select columns).\nSome queryset types completely replace any existing list of select\ncolumns.", "start_line": 1717, "end_line": 1724, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_select", "qualified_name": "set_select", "args": ["self", "cols"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1726, "end_line": 1728, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_distinct_fields", "qualified_name": "add_distinct_fields", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add and resolve the given fields to the query's \"distinct on\" clause.", "start_line": 1730, "end_line": 1735, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_fields", "qualified_name": "add_fields", "args": ["self", "field_names", "allow_m2m"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add the given (model) fields to the select set. Add the field names in\nthe order specified.", "start_line": 1737, "end_line": 1773, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_ordering", "qualified_name": "add_ordering", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add items from the 'ordering' sequence to the query's \"order by\"\nclause. These items are either field names (not column names) --\npossibly with a direction prefix ('-' or '?') -- or OrderBy\nexpressions.\n\nIf 'ordering' is empty, clear all ordering from the query.", "start_line": 1775, "end_line": 1798, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clear_ordering", "qualified_name": "clear_ordering", "args": ["self", "force_empty"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Remove any ordering settings. If 'force_empty' is True, there will be\nno ordering in the resulting query (not even the model's default).", "start_line": 1800, "end_line": 1808, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_group_by", "qualified_name": "set_group_by", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Expand the GROUP BY clause required by the query.\n\nThis will usually be the set of all non-aggregate fields in the\nreturn data. If the database backend supports grouping by the\nprimary key, and the query would be equivalent, the optimization\nwill be made automatically.", "start_line": 1810, "end_line": 1824, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_select_related", "qualified_name": "add_select_related", "args": ["self", "fields"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set up the select_related data structure so that we only select\ncertain related models (as opposed to all models, when\nself.select_related=True).", "start_line": 1826, "end_line": 1840, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_extra", "qualified_name": "add_extra", "args": ["self", "select", "select_params", "where", "params", "tables", "order_by"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add data to the various extra_* attributes for user-created additions\nto the query.", "start_line": 1842, "end_line": 1872, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "clear_deferred_loading", "qualified_name": "clear_deferred_loading", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Remove any fields from the deferred loading set.", "start_line": 1874, "end_line": 1876, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_deferred_loading", "qualified_name": "add_deferred_loading", "args": ["self", "field_names"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add the given list of model field names to the set of fields to\nexclude from loading from the database when automatic column selection\nis done. Add the new field names to any existing field names that\nare deferred (or removed from any existing field names that are marked\nas the only ones for immedia", "start_line": 1878, "end_line": 1896, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_immediate_loading", "qualified_name": "add_immediate_loading", "args": ["self", "field_names"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add the given list of model field names to the set of fields to\nretrieve when the SQL is executed (\"immediate loading\" fields). The\nfield names replace any existing immediate loading field names. If\nthere are field names already specified for deferred loading, remove\nthose names from the new field_n", "start_line": 1898, "end_line": 1920, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_loaded_field_names", "qualified_name": "get_loaded_field_names", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "If any fields are marked to be deferred, return a dictionary mapping\nmodels to a set of names in those fields that will be loaded. If a\nmodel is not in the returned dictionary, none of its fields are\ndeferred.\n\nIf no fields are marked for deferral, return an empty dictionary.", "start_line": 1922, "end_line": 1939, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_loaded_field_names_cb", "qualified_name": "get_loaded_field_names_cb", "args": ["self", "target", "model", "fields"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Callback used by get_deferred_field_names().", "start_line": 1941, "end_line": 1943, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_annotation_mask", "qualified_name": "set_annotation_mask", "args": ["self", "names"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set the mask of annotations that will be returned by the SELECT.", "start_line": 1945, "end_line": 1951, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "append_annotation_mask", "qualified_name": "append_annotation_mask", "args": ["self", "names"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1953, "end_line": 1955, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_extra_mask", "qualified_name": "set_extra_mask", "args": ["self", "names"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Set the mask of extra select items that will be returned by SELECT.\nDon't remove them from the Query since they might be used later.", "start_line": 1957, "end_line": 1966, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "set_values", "qualified_name": "set_values", "args": ["self", "fields"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1968, "end_line": 2001, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "annotation_select", "qualified_name": "annotation_select", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "Return the dictionary of aggregate columns that are not masked and\nshould be used in the SELECT clause. Cache this result for performance.", "start_line": 2004, "end_line": 2020, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "extra_select", "qualified_name": "extra_select", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["property"], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2023, "end_line": 2035, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "trim_start", "qualified_name": "trim_start", "args": ["self", "names_with_path"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Trim joins from the start of the join path. The candidates for trim\nare the PathInfos in names_with_path structure that are m2m joins.\n\nAlso set the select column so the start matches the join.\n\nThis method is meant to be used for generating the subquery joins &\ncols in split_exclude().\n\nReturn a lo", "start_line": 2037, "end_line": 2105, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "is_nullable", "qualified_name": "is_nullable", "args": ["self", "field"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Check if the given field should be treated as nullable.\n\nSome backends treat '' as null and Django treats such fields as\nnullable for those backends. In such situations field.null can be\nFalse even if we should treat the field as nullable.", "start_line": 2107, "end_line": 2123, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "__init__", "qualified_name": "__init__", "args": ["self", "connector", "num_children", "negated"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 2165, "end_line": 2178, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "add_votes", "qualified_name": "add_votes", "args": ["self", "votes"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Add single vote per item to self.votes. Parameter can be any\niterable.", "start_line": 2180, "end_line": 2185, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "update_join_types", "qualified_name": "update_join_types", "args": ["self", "query"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Change join types so that the generated query is as efficient as\npossible, but still correct. So, change as many joins as possible\nto INNER, but don't make OUTER joins INNER if that could remove\nresults from the query.", "start_line": 2187, "end_line": 2241, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "prefix_gen", "qualified_name": "prefix_gen", "args": [], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Generate a sequence of characters in alphabetical order:\n    -> 'A', 'B', 'C', ...\n\nWhen the alphabet is finished, the sequence will continue with the\nCartesian product:\n    -> 'AA', 'AB', 'AC', ...", "start_line": 840, "end_line": 856, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "final_transformer", "qualified_name": "final_transformer", "args": [