select", "order_by"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of 2-tuples of form (sql, params).\n\nThe logic of what exactly the GROUP BY clause contains is hard\nto describe in other words than \"if it passes the test suite,\nthen it is correct\".", "start_line": 57, "end_line": 137, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "collapse_group_by", "qualified_name": "collapse_group_by", "args": ["self", "expressions", "having"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 139, "end_line": 183, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_select", "qualified_name": "get_select", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return three values:\n- a list of 3-tuples of (expression, (sql, params), alias)\n- a klass_info structure,\n- a dictionary of annotations\n\nThe (sql, params) is what the expression will produce, and alias is the\n\"AS alias\" for the column (possibly None).\n\nThe klass_info structure contains the following", "start_line": 185, "end_line": 253, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_order_by", "qualified_name": "get_order_by", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of 2-tuples of form (expr, (sql, params, is_ref)) for the\nORDER BY clause.\n\nThe order_by clause can alter the select clause (for example it\ncan add aliases to clauses that do not yet have one, or it can\nadd totally new select clauses).", "start_line": 255, "end_line": 364, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_extra_select", "qualified_name": "get_extra_select", "args": ["self", "order_by", "select"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 366, "end_line": 374, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "quote_name_unless_alias", "qualified_name": "quote_name_unless_alias", "args": ["self", "name"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "A wrapper around connection.ops.quote_name that doesn't quote aliases\nfor table names. This avoids problems with some SQL dialects that treat\nquoted strings specially (e.g. PostgreSQL).", "start_line": 376, "end_line": 391, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "compile", "qualified_name": "compile", "args": ["self", "node", "select_format"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 393, "end_line": 401, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_combinator_sql", "qualified_name": "get_combinator_sql", "args": ["self", "combinator", "all"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 403, "end_line": 455, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "as_sql", "qualified_name": "as_sql", "args": ["self", "with_limits", "with_col_aliases"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Create the SQL for this query. Return the SQL string and list of\nparameters.\n\nIf 'with_limits' is False, any limit/offset information is not included\nin the query.", "start_line": 457, "end_line": 617, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_default_columns", "qualified_name": "get_default_columns", "args": ["self", "start_alias", "opts", "from_parent"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Compute the default columns for selecting every field in the base\nmodel. Will sometimes be called to pull in related models (e.g. via\nselect_related), in which case \"opts\" and \"start_alias\" will be given\nto provide a starting point for the traversal.\n\nReturn a list of strings, quoted appropriately f", "start_line": 619, "end_line": 661, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_distinct", "qualified_name": "get_distinct", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a quoted list of fields to use in DISTINCT ON part of the query.\n\nThis method can alter the tables in the query, and thus it must be\ncalled before get_from_clause().", "start_line": 663, "end_line": 685, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "find_ordering_name", "qualified_name": "find_ordering_name", "args": ["self", "name", "opts", "alias", "default_order", "already_seen"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return the table alias (the name might be ambiguous, the alias will\nnot be) and column name for ordering by the given 'name' parameter.\nThe 'name' is of the form 'field1__field2__...__fieldN'.", "start_line": 687, "end_line": 716, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "_setup_joins", "qualified_name": "_setup_joins", "args": ["self", "pieces", "opts", "alias"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Helper method for get_order_by() and get_distinct().\n\nget_ordering() and get_distinct() must produce same target columns on\nsame input, as the prefixes of get_ordering() and get_distinct() must\nmatch. Executing SQL where this is not true is an error.", "start_line": 718, "end_line": 729, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_from_clause", "qualified_name": "get_from_clause", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a list of strings that are joined together to go after the\n\"FROM\" part of the query, as well as a list any extra parameters that\nneed to be included. Subclasses, can override this to create a\nfrom-clause via a \"select\".\n\nThis should only be called after any SQL construction methods that\nmight", "start_line": 731, "end_line": 763, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_related_selections", "qualified_name": "get_related_selections", "args": ["self", "select", "opts", "root_alias", "cur_depth", "requested", "restricted"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Fill in the information needed for a select_related query. The current\ndepth is measured as the number of connections away from the root model\n(for example, cur_depth=1 means we are looking at models with direct\nconnections to the root model).", "start_line": 765, "end_line": 936, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_select_for_update_of_arguments", "qualified_name": "get_select_for_update_of_arguments", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return a quoted list of arguments for the SELECT FOR UPDATE OF part of\nthe query.", "start_line": 938, "end_line": 995, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "deferred_to_columns", "qualified_name": "deferred_to_columns", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Convert the self.deferred_loading data structure to mapping of table\nnames to sets of column names which are to be loaded. Return the\ndictionary.", "start_line": 997, "end_line": 1005, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "get_converters", "qualified_name": "get_converters", "args": ["self", "expressions"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1007, "end_line": 1015, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "apply_converters", "qualified_name": "apply_converters", "args": ["self", "rows", "converters"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1017, "end_line": 1026, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "results_iter", "qualified_name": "results_iter", "args": ["self", "results", "tuple_expected", "chunked_fetch", "chunk_size"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Return an iterator over the results from executing this query.", "start_line": 1028, "end_line": 1040, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "has_results", "qualified_name": "has_results", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Backends (e.g. NoSQL) can override this in order to use optimized\nversions of \"query has any results.\"", "start_line": 1042, "end_line": 1050, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "execute_sql", "qualified_name": "execute_sql", "args": ["self", "result_type", "chunked_fetch", "chunk_size"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Run the query against the database and return the result(s). The\nreturn value is a single data item if result_type is SINGLE, or an\niterator over the results if the result_type is MULTI.\n\nresult_type is either MULTI (use fetchmany() to retrieve all rows),\nSINGLE (only retrieve a single row), or None", "start_line": 1052, "end_line": 1117, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "as_subquery_condition", "qualified_name": "as_subquery_condition", "args": ["self", "alias", "columns", "compiler"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1119, "end_line": 1130, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "explain_query", "qualified_name": "explain_query", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 1132, "end_line": 1140, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "field_as_sql", "qualified_name": "field_as_sql", "args": ["self", "field", "val"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Take a field and a value intended to be saved on that field, and\nreturn placeholder SQL and accompanying params. Check for raw values,\nexpressions, and fields with get_placeholder() defined in that order.\n\nWhen field is None, consider the value raw and use it as the\nplaceholder, with no correspondin", "start_line": 1146, "end_line": 1176, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "prepare_value", "qualified_name": "prepare_value", "args": ["self", "field", "value"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Prepare a value to be used in a query by resolving it if it is an\nexpression and otherwise calling the field's get_db_prep_save().", "start_line": 1178, "end_line": 1199, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "pre_save_val", "qualified_name": "pre_save_val", "args": ["self", "field", "obj"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Get the given field's value off the given obj. pre_save() is used for\nthings like auto_now on DateTimeField. Skip it if this is a raw query.", "start_line": 1201, "end_line": 1208, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "assemble_as_sql", "qualified_name": "assemble_as_sql", "args": ["self", "fields", "value_rows"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "Take a sequence of N fields and a sequence of M rows of values, and\ngenerate placeholder SQL and parameters for each field and value.\nReturn a pair containing:\n * a sequence of M rows of N SQL placeholder strin