rimary_key", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "If an existing primary key is specified with different values for other\nfields, then IntegrityError is raised and data isn't updated.", "start_line": 472, "end_line": 480, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_updates_in_transaction", "qualified_name": "test_updates_in_transaction", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["skipUnlessDBFeature('has_select_for_update')", "skipUnlessDBFeature('supports_transactions')"], "docstring": "Objects are selected and updated in a transaction to avoid race\nconditions. This test forces update_or_create() to hold the lock\nin another thread for a relatively long time so that it can update\nwhile it holds the lock. The updated field isn't a field in 'defaults',\nso update_or_create() shouldn't ", "start_line": 488, "end_line": 538, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_creation_in_transaction", "qualified_name": "test_creation_in_transaction", "args": ["self"], "decorators": ["skipUnlessDBFeature('has_select_for_update')", "skipUnlessDBFeature('supports_transactions')"], "docstring": "Objects are selected and updated in a transaction to avoid race\nconditions. This test checks the behavior of update_or_create() when\nthe object doesn't already exist, but another thread creates the\nobject before update_or_create() does and then attempts to update the\nobject, also before update_or_cr", "start_line": 542, "end_line": 596, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_get_or_create_with_invalid_defaults", "qualified_name": "test_get_or_create_with_invalid_defaults", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 604, "end_line": 606, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name": "test_get_or_create_with_invalid_kwargs", "qualified_name": "test_get_or_create_with_invalid_kwargs", "args": ["self"], "decorators": [], "docstring": "", "start_line": 608, "end_line": 610, "is_async": false, "is_method": false}, {"name